  "id": "wandering-attention",
  "term": "wandering attention",
  "definition": "Wandering attention is attention that shifts among ideas or objects without a coherent connection, so the mind does not stay steadily on one topic. In this historical usage, it contrasts with sustained attention, where thoughts link together in an orderly way and keep the same subject before the mind.",
